# Go CLI

## Layout

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `internal/cli/` | Cobra command groups |
| `internal/clierror` | Exit-code contract (ops 1–5, policy 10/20) |
| `internal/verdict` | Scan result envelope |
| `internal/cmdutil` | `--fail-on`, `--block-on`, `--output`, `--raw` (default), `--envelope` |
| `internal/config` | Auth and endpoint (flags > env > TOML) |
| `internal/embedded/python` | Go ↔ embedded CPython bridge (see embedded-python rule) |
| `api/` | HTTP client — extend, don't duplicate |

## Quality gates

Run after Go changes:

```bash
go build ./...
go vet ./...
go test ./...
```

## Patterns

- Propagate errors; map to `internal/clierror` at command boundary — no magic `os.Exit` in libraries
- Table-driven tests for flags, exit codes, and JSON output shape
- HTTP client: timeouts on all outbound calls; validate user-supplied URLs before fetch
- Use build tags where needed (`stub` vs full embed for Python); document tag matrix in comments or docs
- No `shared/pkg` — this is a standalone repo

